CM ============================================================
CM  TM-SC-NEC-006: Screwdriver Antenna — 30m Band
CM  2.4m whip, base loading coil, 4 horizontal elevated radials
CM  Frequency: 10.100–10.150 MHz (5 points, 0.013 MHz step)
CM
CM  Loading coil (series RL at base, segment 1 of GW1):
CM    R = 1.927 ohm  (Rcoil = Xant / Q, Q~300)
CM    X = 578 ohm    (XL required to resonate 2.4m whip on 30m)
CM
CM  Whip: 2.4m, avg radius 0.006m, 20 segments
CM  Radials: 4 x 2.4m at z=0.005m, 90 deg spacing
CM  Ground: real (Sommerfeld-Norton), eps=13, sigma=0.005
CM  Feed: 1V voltage source at GW1, seg 1
CM
CM  Tuning note: 30m is WARC-only, no SSB, CW/data only.
CM  Band is only 50 kHz wide (10.100-10.150 MHz). SWR bandwidth
CM  of loaded whip at this frequency is very narrow; motor tuning
CM  must step slowly near resonance. Whip is 24.1% of QW (9.94m).
CM  Efficiency noticeably reduced vs higher bands; loading coil
CM  loss dominates. Consider higher Q coil construction for 30m.
